WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.560
Shake a ripe maize tassel and a yellow haze drifts off.

2
00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:09.520
Each grain is a tiny plant of three cells.

3
00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:13.820
If it lands on a silk, it grows a tube and delivers two sperm.

4
00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:16.500
Both sperm normally fertilize something.

5
00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:18.460
Why two?

6
00:00:18.983 --> 00:00:21.763
Pollination is the transfer of pollen to a stigma.

7
00:00:22.763 --> 00:00:27.203
Fertilization is the fusion of a sperm with a female cell inside the ovule.

8
00:00:28.003 --> 00:00:29.083
They are separate events.

9
00:00:29.903 --> 00:00:33.243
The grain grows a pollen tube down through the style into the ovary.

10
00:00:34.023 --> 00:00:37.023
The sperm have no flagella, so they ride inside the tube.

11
00:00:37.943 --> 00:00:41.623
Near the ovule, the tube follows chemical signals from the synergids.

12
00:00:42.343 --> 00:00:45.423
It bursts into one synergid and releases both sperm.

13
00:00:46.417 --> 00:00:50.437
Now count chromosomes in maize, which has 20 in its body cells.

14
00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:52.317
The egg carries 10.

15
00:00:53.157 --> 00:00:54.297
Each sperm carries 10.

16
00:00:55.157 --> 00:00:59.637
The central cell is a large cell of the embryo sac, with two polar nuclei.

17
00:01:00.497 --> 00:01:01.817
10 + 10 makes 20.

18
00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:04.640
One sperm fuses with the egg.

19
00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:09.280
10 + 10 makes 20. That zygote grows into the embryo.

20
00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:12.500
The other sperm fuses with the central cell.

21
00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:19.380
20 + 10 makes 30. This is the first cell of the endosperm, a tissue that stores food

22
00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:20.380
for the embryo.

23
00:01:21.133 --> 00:01:22.593
Now count the sets of 10.

24
00:01:23.493 --> 00:01:26.593
The embryo has one maternal set and one paternal set.

25
00:01:27.433 --> 00:01:30.693
The endosperm has two maternal sets and one paternal set.

26
00:01:31.513 --> 00:01:34.993
The seed coat grows from the integuments, which are the mother's own tissue.

27
00:01:35.893 --> 00:01:36.893
It carries 20.

28
00:01:37.817 --> 00:01:42.277
Cross a maize plant with two white alleles with pollen from a plant with two yellow

29
00:01:42.277 --> 00:01:47.677
alleles. The embryo has one white allele and one yellow, and the endosperm has two

30
00:01:47.677 --> 00:01:49.177
white alleles and one yellow.

31
00:01:50.117 --> 00:01:53.057
Assuming yellow is fully dominant, the kernels are yellow.

32
00:01:53.957 --> 00:01:55.017
This is called xenia.

33
00:01:55.817 --> 00:02:00.617
Keep the rule: two maternal sets and one paternal set make the endosperm, and one of

34
00:02:00.617 --> 00:02:01.517
each make the embryo.
